Access Softek is a recognized name with an established reputation in the LLVM community.
From early on in LLVM’s origins, we have worked on a number of projects such as a front-end compiler, back-end code generation / optimizations, linkers, code instrumentation, and did so with a focus of targeting different platforms - from well-known platforms to those that are new, quite unique and not yet publicly available.
We "own" and host the LLVM Lab, and orchestrate the continued integration (LLVM buildbot) for all projects under the LLVM umbrella.
We are growing our team, and are looking for experienced Compiler Engineers to work on the LLVM and Clang based toolchain. Our product is a set of instruments that includes the Clang compiler, a linker, tools, and libraries adapted and optimized to build safe, efficient applications.

As a member of the toolchain team, you will:
• analyze the requirements, research, design, enhance and implement different components of the toolchain to meet the clients needs;
• extend the open source LLVM, Clang, binutils code bases to support the client's platform;
• closely collaborate with the LLVM community and contribute public patches to the LLVM and Clang repository;
• analyze, build and debug the platform code and platform specific tests, analyze and identify system level issues;
• develop new and maintain the existing target specific tests.
Required qualifications:
• expert knowledge of C/C++;
• experience in overall design of compilers, code generation and optimization;
• cross-compilation using GCC or Clang;
• in-depth understanding of multithreading, object-oriented analysis and design;
• version control systems;
• good self-motivation, ability to work independently;
• strong track record of building high performance, production quality software;
• passion for writing clean and effective code;
• good English, strong communication and teamwork skills.
Nice to have qualifications:
• knowledge of the C++11 / C++14/C++17 features;
• knowledge of assemblers, linkers, object file formats, debuggers and experience using them;
• familiarity with *nix tools, CMake, make;
• scripting languages such as Python and bash.
Our benefits:
• Work from anywhere in the world!
• Flexible working hours
• Experienced development teams
• Long-term employment
• Competitive salary
• Paid vacation and days off on national holidays
• Paid sick leave and internal medical insurance policy
• Mental health coverage
• Global corporate events for all staff
• Compensation for training and additional education
• Community of practice, regular knowledge sharing among colleagues
• Provision of computer equipment
• Internet compensation (50$ per month)
• Relocation compensation package to be discussed individually
• And other benefits, described in detail in the Staff Handbook

Spektrum supports apex purchasers (NATO, UN, EU, and National Government and Defence) and their Tier 1 supplier ecosystem with a wide range of specialist services. We provide our clients with professional services, specialised aerospace and defence sales, delivery, and operational subject matter expertise. We are looking for personnel to join our team and support key client projects.

Who we are supporting:

The NATO Communication and Information Agency (NCIA) is responsible for providing secure and effective communications and information technology (IT) services to NATO's member countries and its partners. The agency was established in 2012 and is headquartered in Brussels, Belgium.

The NCIA provides a wide range of services, including:

• Cyber Security: The NCIA provides advanced cybersecurity solutions to protect NATO's communication networks and information systems against cyber threats.
• Command and Control Systems: The NCIA develops and maintains the systems used by NATO's military commanders to plan and execute operations.
• Satellite Communications: The NCIA provides satellite communications services to enable secure and reliable communications between NATO forces.
• Electronic Warfare: The NCIA provides electronic warfare services to support NATO's mission to detect, deny, and defeat threats to its communication networks.
• Information Management: The NCIA manages NATO's information technology infrastructure, including its databases, applications, and servers.

Overall, the NCIA plays a critical role in ensuring the security and effectiveness of NATO's communication and information technology capabilities.

The program:

Assistance and Advisory Service (AAS):

The NATO Communications and Information Agency (NCI Agency) is NATO’s principal C3 capability deliverer and CIS service provider. It provides, maintains and defends the NATO enterprise-wide information technology infrastructure to enable Allies to consult together under Article IV, and, when required, stand together in the face of attack under Article V.

To provide these critical services, in the modern evolving dynamic environment the NCI Agency needs to build and maintain high performance-engaged workforce. The NCI Agency workforce strategically consists of three major categorise's: NATO International Civilians (NIC)'s, Military (Mil), and Interim Workforce Consultants (IWC)'s. The IWCs are a critical part of the overall NCI Agency workforce and make up approximately 15 percent of the total workforce.

Role ID – 2026-0136:

Role Duties and Responsibilities:

• Technical documentation development
• Characterization of BLOS AP use cases, in accordance to the BRIPES service delivery concept, and definition of configuration baselines;
• Prepare and maintain technical documentation containing the STANAG 5066 complete protocol stack parameters and configuration required for the implementation of BRASS Enhancement 1 services;
• Interoperability analysis on different implementations of STANAGs, namely STANAG 4538 and 5066, and documentation of discrepancies found in the configuration of different Editions of those STANAGs.
• Optimization of configuration baselines based on identified performance criteria;
• Ensure technical documentation is complete, consistent, traceable, and aligned with applicable NATO standards and NCIA engineering practices;
• Identify configuration dependencies resulting from different STANAG editions, vendor implementation specificities, and national implementation approaches;
• Maintain version control and configuration management of all engineering documentation and technical artefacts.
• Testing and validation activities
• Setup of a testing environment for verification and validation of configuration baselines, including modems back-to-back, usage of HF channel simulators and over-the-air transmission;
• Analysis on interoperability and interfacing challenges between STANAG 5066 and interfacing modules part of the IP over HF architecture. This includes troubleshooting of identified standard interface issues and conformance testing.
• Develop testing approaches and validation plans supporting the implementation of BRASS Enhancement 1 services;
• Participation, as requested, in experimentation and demonstration activities in events held within NATO countries. Configure and validate service parameters using NCIA reference systems and laboratory equipment, simulated HF environments, and, where required, over-the-air testing capabilities;
• Support the establishment and maintenance of representative testing environments for the verification and validation of BRASS Enhancement 1 service configurations;
• Perform technical testing and interoperability validation of service configurations prior to publication of implementation guidance;
• Analyse test results, identify interoperability issues, configuration inconsistencies, and implementation risks;
• Recommend corrective actions and optimized service configurations where required;
• Document testing activities, validation results, engineering findings, and recommendations.
• Service Instructions development
• Development of Service Instructions for BRIPES, including full protocol stack for the different information services, i.e. formal messaging (ACP 127 and STANAG 4406 Annex E), e-mail, chat and web services;
• Ensure Service Instructions are aligned with the technical documentation, validated configurations, and applicable NATO standards;
• Maintain consistency between Service Instructions, technical documentation, and approved implementation baselines;
• Update Service Instructions following validation activities, stakeholder feedback, or changes to technical requirements.
• Engineering analysis and technical support
• Perform engineering assessments of proposed service configurations and implementation approaches;
• Analyse interoperability impacts associated with differing STANAG 5066 editions, vendor-specific implementations, and national deployment environments;
• Analyse interoperability and interface challenges affecting the BRIPES architecture and provide recommendations to resolve identified issues;
• Provide engineering recommendations supporting harmonized implementation across NATO Nations;
• Support technical coordination with NCIA stakeholders and other NATO organizations involved in BRASS Enhancement 1 implementation;
• Contribute engineering expertise to implementation planning, technical reviews, and working groups as required.
• Stakeholder coordination and reporting
• Liaise with NCIA technical authorities and relevant NATO stakeholders, providing engineering inputs and consolidated technical documentation;
• Prepare technical reports, engineering analyses, implementation guidance, and briefing material;
• Participate in technical meetings, workshops, validation activities, and engineering reviews, technical demonstrations, and experimentation activities as required;
• Report progress, technical risks, issues, and recommendations in accordance with NCIA governance processes.

Essential Skills, Experience and Certifications:

• University Degree in Telecommunications, Electronics, Computer Engineering,
• Information Technology, or a related field, with at least two (2) years of post-related experience; or Higher Vocational Training with a minimum of five (5) years of post-related experience;
• Minimum of two (2) years of practical experience in the engineering, implementation, configuration, or support of military or secure communications systems; Assigned personnel shall have a solid scientific background and with a proven track record of technical management work in the area of IP over HF services based on STANAG 5066.
• Demonstrated knowledge of STANAG 5066 Ed 3 and Ed 4, including its protocol stack, implementation considerations, and interoperability aspects.
• Knowledge on the usage of standards associated with IP over HF services, namely STANAG 4538 and STANAG 4539;
• Knowledge on the usage and interfacing commercial and/or open-source application clients with STANAG 5066, namely in the areas of formal messaging (ACP127, STANAG 4406 Annex E, ACP142), e-mail, chat and web services.
• Expertise in developing STANAG 5066-based testbeds and test setups applying the different STANAG 5066 configurations and modes of operation.
• Demonstrated capability in performing interoperability testing activities, namely in international forums, using STANAG 5066 testbed. This includes experience in coordinating interoperability test scenarios and performing interoperability analysis reporting.
• Demonstrated knowledge and understanding of Use Cases applying STANAG 5066, namely in the NATO Maritime Forces domain.
• Strong knowledge of IP networking principles, communication protocols, and network architectures, including protocol stack configuration and interoperability
• considerations;
• Experience in the preparation of technical documentation, engineering specifications, implementation guidance, or Service Instructions for communication systems;
• Experience in testing, validation, and troubleshooting of communication systems, including analysis of technical issues and implementation of corrective actions;
• Experience in developing or supporting engineering test environments and interoperability testing activities for communication systems is desirable;
• Good understanding of interoperability principles, configuration management, and engineering practices supporting multinational or multi-vendor communication environments;
• Familiarity with relevant NATO communications standards, STANAGs, and secure communications architectures;
• Experience working with laboratory environments, reference systems, or engineering test platforms for the validation of communication services is desirable.
• Experience in NATO or multinational military environments is strongly desirable;
• Solid understanding of NATO operational standards, procedures, and communication protocols;
• Experience supporting engineering activities related to military communication systems, technical documentation, interoperability, or implementation of communication services;
• Strong analytical capability applied to technical assessments, interoperability analysis, testing, validation, and engineering activities;
• Experience coordinating technical activities with multiple stakeholders and contributing to technical meetings, workshops, or multinational working groups is desirable;
• Experience collecting, analysing, and consolidating technical information from multiple sources into engineering documentation and technical reports is desirable;
• English language proficiency at minimum C1 level. Communicating effectively in
• English both in writing and orally, with excellent writing and briefing skills to different types of audiences (including senior technical and non-technical stakeholders), and writing high-quality technical reports for NATO circulation.
• Strong communication skills, with the ability to clearly articulate complex technical communication and interoperability concepts;
• Strong interpersonal skills, enabling effective collaboration with technical teams and stakeholders;
• Ability to work independently with minimal supervision while contributing effectively as part of a team;
• Strong analytical and problem-solving capabilities;
• Ability to engage constructively with stakeholders, identify technical issues, and recommend practical engineering solutions;
• High level of motivation, adaptability, and collaboration.
• Knowledge of NATO and NCIA structures, roles, and organisational context is desirable.

Working Policy:

• 100% Remote

Travel:

• Some travel to other NATO sites may be required

Security Clearance:

• Valid National or NATO Secret personal security clearance
